@ 29.1.1.1.4 - Proto-Athabaskan to Chilcotin
# citation: Whimemsz, from Krauss, Michael and Victor Golla (1981), “Northern Athapaskan Languages”. Handbook of North American Indians, Vol. 6 (Subarctic), 67 – 85
	# TS series desibilantizes
	V > {Vˀ,V[+RTR]}
	{TŠ,TŠʷ} K > TS TŠ
	# The Q series incompletely moves to the K series, the latter being more common
	e {ɑ,ə} > i {e,ɪ}
	Vˀ > V[+high tone]